			<div class="content" id="post-content-1518318">
									

<p>Doesn't stop moving. It stops going after the closest organism looking at it and instead only goes after the closest organism until it has contacted three. After that it goes after the closest one observing it again. It's a matter of losing one D-class a month instead of three, and also not endangering containment due to the temporary imbalance.</p>
<p>Kappa events are mostly just a nuisance but they have the potential to make things much worse if they happen at an inopportune time. They basically happen because it starts to get &quot;hungry&quot; enough not to care.</p>

