<p>First, If the light doesn't reflect and is visible through anything, doesn't that mean that it can be seen from anywhere on Earth? People in China see this tiny little beam of light shining straight up through the ground and moving in a circle. I don't think that it would be possible to contain knowledge of this thing, as-is. Maybe add something about the light atenuating over distance despite its lack of refraction/reflection?</p>
<p>Second, the worst case scenario containment procedure seems to be to launch it into space. This seems like a terrible idea to me. It would be like shooting a flare that never burns out, it's pretty much gauranteed to be seen and paid attention to by a vast number of civilians, and then all hope of knowing where it will go is out the window.</p>
